# Docker related files
# Root-relative patterns match only the context root, so a bare `.env` left apps/api/.env,
# apps/api/.env.test, apps/mobile/.env and apps/web-player/.env.development in every build
# context. They never reached a production image — the final stages copy named artifacts rather
# than the tree — but they did land in the `COPY . .` layer of the build stage, which is exported
# to the registry as build cache.
**/.env
**/.env.*
nginx/logs/
backups/

# Dependencies
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
npm-debug.log
yarn-error.log
pnpm-debug.log

# Development
*.log

# Build outputs. Prefixed with **/ for the same reason as the env files above: a root-relative
# pattern matches only the context root, so a bare `.next/` left apps/*/.next and packages/*/dist
# in the context. That shipped a local dev build into the production image and sent gigabytes of
# artifacts to the daemon on every build — apps/ alone is 2.3 GB with them.
**/dist/
**/build/
**/.next/
**/out/
# Nitro's bundle for apps/web-artists. Measured at 217 MB on a developer checkout, and a stale
# copy of it landed in the build stage's `COPY . .` right before the real build overwrote it.
**/.output/
**/coverage/
**/.turbo/
**/test-results/
**/playwright-report/
apps/desktop/src-tauri/target/
graphify-out/

# The repository history. Nothing in any Dockerfile reads it, and at 31 GB on a developer
# checkout it was the build context: `docker build` transferred 11.7 GB before this line existed
# and had not finished. A CI checkout is shallow, so this mattered locally first — but a shallow
# .git still carries every blob of the checked-out tree and still reaches the daemon for nothing.
.git/

# Developer-local scratch space and agent tooling. None of it is read by a build.
.br-scratch/
.claude/
.impeccable/

# Seeded media for apps/api. The directory's own .gitignore keeps everything but the .gitkeep
# placeholders out of git, so CI never sees it — but a developer checkout carries 823 MB of
# downloaded tracks here and apps/api/Dockerfile copies the tree wholesale. The runtime storage
# root is /app/storage (a named volume), which is a different path entirely.
apps/api/storage/private/

# Keep example file
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.sample
!**/.env.template
